[Music]  welcome to part two of this seven part  mini series  in which we visualize the paths taken by  the various key figures during the  events of the great calamity if you  haven't watched the previous part which  covers link and zelda  be sure to check that one out first as  we will skip some of the introduction  established in that part  in this episode i will be joined by  hyrulegamer we have been wanting to  collaborate for a while now and fate  once again meddled with our plans when  hyrule warrior's age of calamity was  unexpectedly announced  however we will persevere so i decided  to cover this one with him at my side  after you're done watching this video be  sure to head over to his channel and  check out his video about the unseen  parts from breath the wild which we will  see in their prime in age of calamity  as always a link will be in the  description and in the end card  just like last time we will be pausing  the narrative at specific moments to  inject a suggestion for a possible  gameplay section  now without further ado let's jump right  back into it  as soon as rivali witnessed the honors  of the calamity from afar and reported  ganon's return to the rest of the party  the first priority for the four pilots  was of course to make their way to each  of their respective divine beasts  arbosa tags along with lincoln zelda  through the promenade the canyons and  then kakariko village  still accompanied by lincoln zelda they  make their way down to sahasrara slow at  which point she parts ways with the hero  and princess  her goal is to meet up with van the  boris who is located in the vast sancy  of her home province the gerudo desert  which isn't exactly close especially on  foot  when link and zelda turn right at the  bottom of the sahasrara slope  erbosa takes the left path across the  aegis bridge  from there she treks past battery lake  and takes the allen bridge to reach the  east point and  subsequently moves west along the foot  of the great plateau  past the other outposts located there  it's safe to say that the paths the  champions will traverse towards their  divine beasts will be important  and depicted for gameplay the many  outposts which span across the edge of  the great plateau played a crucial role  during the calamity as it is for here  that the evacuation line towards forte  tenno was made possible  with soldiers creating a defensive line  and keeping the fleeing citizens safe in  the process  since herbosa crossed right through this  section it is possible that she played  an important role in helping to defend  the outposts well  on her way to vanda boris although it is  likely too early at this point for any  guardians to have arrived here  we have seen that monsters such as the  coblins and moblins also took part in  the attack  in breath of the wild the ruins of these  outposts are crawling with monsters  so it's not too far-fetched to assume  that the initial defense of the outposts  was against monsters  rather than guardians after potentially  assisting the hylians at the outposts  urbosa continues on her way to gerudo  desert she follows the road that passes  by the great plateau  then heads south across the dig dog  suspension bridge  and into gerudo canyon pass from there  she moves through the grudo canyon to  make her way towards the desert gerudo  canyon is a path without any branching  paths  there's a good chance that this will be  a playable section as well  since it's a great way to force a linear  style of battling your way through the  narrow canyon  if the previous scenario turns out to be  true and herbosa did indeed help with  the defense of the outposts at the great  plateau this would also justify the  presence of guardians inside the canyon  as by this point they could have arrived  this far from the castle in pursuit of  verbosa  and her divine beast now this is where  we come to a point where the game might  ignore some of the information provided  by creating a champion  and comes up with its own version of  events in the age of calamity trailer we  see her  fighting yiga clan members in gerudo  town not only that but she's wearing her  blue champion's cloth while doing it  something she didn't receive until right  before the great calamity  i think it's unlikely that herbosa would  take such a massive detour only to  return to spectacle rock afterwards  getting to her divine beast is the main  objective and of utmost importance in  the strategy to fight ganon  with this possible inconsistency we are  going to cover two different options  both of which have evidence supporting  it option one would be that the attack  on gerudo town despite the presence of  the champion's cloth  still takes place before the calamity at  the very least one day before  since on the actual day of the calamity  she's at the promenade nowhere close to  the gerudo region  in this case the path laid out by  creating a champion stays true  she moves up the quarry at the end of  the canyon and straight up the spectacle  rock  this section would probably still fall  under the gameplay scenario mentioned  earlier  where you fight your way through the  canyon then up to quarry and towards  vanoborus  the evidence supporting this lies in the  many dead guardians found at both the  quarry and atop the mountains on the way  to spectacle rock  the only thing working against it is the  fact that they are also found way beyond  spectacle rock on the other side  of the mountains close to the lommei  labyrinth option two would be that the  attack on gerudo town does take place  during the calamity if this is indeed  true we have to come up with a  possibility as to why urbosa would  travel all the way out here rather than  to spectacle rock when there's so little  time to lose  in which case i proposed that vana boris  may not be located on spectacle rock  initially but rather close to gerudo  town  and this would make sense since nobody  knew when ganon was going to show up  and in the days and weeks before the  champions had been practicing to get  their beasts under control  spectacle rock isn't exactly the most  ideal location to do this since its peak  is quite narrow with very little room  for movement  instead it would be more effective to  use the huge open space of the desert to  perform these kinds of exercises  it's also noteworthy that in this memory  we actually see vonne boris parked in  the desert which gives some credence to  this theory  but i want to reiterate that if the  attack on gerudo town indeed takes place  before the great calamity  starts then the next gameplay scenario  is basically useless  and we can just skip right to vanna  boris on spectacle rock  with this new path in mind urbosa makes  her way to her divine beast only to  realize that garuda town is under yiga  attack  while her task as pilot of vanna boris  is crucial she is also the chief of  gerudo  as such she probably wouldn't leave her  people to their fate and  may decide to join the battle briefly to  help defend their home and keep the  civilians out of harm's way  after disposing of most of the yiga and  letting the gerudo army take care of the  rest she boards van the boris and takes  her up to spectacle rock  with her powerful laser ready to take  aim and fire ganon uses his malice to  corrupt van the boris  trapping urbosa inside to make matters  worse the malice which infects the giant  machine  manifests into the monstrous phantom  we've come to know is thunder blight  ganon  we could put this next part up as a  possible gameplay scenario but i think  it's pretty  safe to say that this won't be necessary  it would be very strange if the actual  fight between  urbosa and thunder blight wasn't  playable so we're just going to assume  it will be  and we all know how this is going to end  after a fierce battle between the  phantom and champion herbosa is  eventually bested by ganon's puppet and  killed in the process  her spirit is trapped within the walls  of the very machine she was destined to  pilot  here she will linger for the next 100  years  arbosa's crow fate is just one of the  many sad moments awaiting us in age of  calamity  she fought valiantly and gave it her all  but the unexpected turn of events at the  hands of calamity ganon caught her off  guard  and it won't be until 100 years later  when link wakes up that she will finally  get the chance to take revenge on the  monster which took her life away  so unexpectedly  [Music]  hmm  you

